# CommentsService — Change log

[English](change.log) · [Русский](change.log.ru) · [Українська](change.log.ua)

## 1.1.0.3 OnionArchitecture — 2026-10-29

Branch: `CommentsService/v_1.1.0.3_OnionArchitecture`

- Added Application referencing Domain only, with application-owned ICommentRepository and IUnitOfWork ports; core contracts expose no EF/HTTP/provider types.
- Implemented the repository in Infrastructure; repository and unit of work share one scoped DbContext. Application use cases/HTTP comment features remain scheduled for 1.1.0.4.
- Moved migrations and snapshot to Infrastructure/Persistence/Migrations, retaining migration 20261029195935_InitialDataModel, its SQL and history. No replacement migration or checkpoint rotation.
- Moved HTTP mappings to Api/Endpoints and connected database readiness through a standard IHealthCheck adapter. Technical migration/status contracts remain outside the application core.
- Updated architecture tests for inward references, independent Domain/Application assemblies, provider-free port signatures and HTTP endpoint boundaries.
- Added repository/unit-of-work integration checks with transaction rollback. Updated Docker, solution, three READMEs, read.me, architecture/schema/migration documents and plans.
- Validation: Release solution build has zero warnings/errors; 21 domain/architecture and 10 PostgreSQL tests passed (31 total).
- Verified identical migration SQL, no pending model changes, retained live schema/history/data/relationships, environment, previous recovery copies and persistent volumes across deployment.
- Verified fresh installation from the relocated migration, image migrate/check commands, database/process health, API metadata/frontend/API 404 and Development health 503 with missing/unreachable DB.
- Edge desktop/360 px checks passed. Visual Studio GUI opening and MySQL Workbench GUI import remain unverified.
- Version stays 1.1.0.3; next planned iteration remains 1.1.0.4 CommentsApi.

## 1.1.0.3 BackendLayers — 2026-10-29

Branch: `CommentsService/v_1.1.0.3_BackendLayers`

- Replaced the single-project backend structure with Domain, Infrastructure and Api projects; version remains 1.1.0.3.
- Domain/Entities has no project/package dependencies; constructors protect required values and bounds, keep author/comment links consistent, and expose read-only collections.
- Infrastructure owns Persistence/CommentsDbContext, separate Persistence/Configurations, the design-time factory and Migrations.
- API delegates readiness/migration operations through small injected interfaces; EF/provider logic and entity mappings no longer reside in API.
- Preserved migration 20261029195935_InitialDataModel, its generated SQL, history and physical schema. Updated CLR namespaces in migration metadata; no replacement migration or checkpoint rotation.
- Split tests into domain/architecture and database projects. Architecture tests enforce dependency direction and a persistence/HTTP-free domain; database tests verify read-only navigation materialization and transaction rollback.
- Updated solution references, Docker restore/publish steps, three READMEs, read.me, architecture/schema/migration documents and plans.
- Validation: Release solution build has zero warnings/errors; 18 domain/architecture tests and 8 PostgreSQL integration tests passed (26 total).
- Verified identical generated SQL, no pending EF model changes, unchanged live schema/history/data/relationships, private environment and volumes across update; only owned retention fixtures were removed.
- Verified initial installation using the moved migration in a separate blank database, container migration/check commands, HTTP readiness/status/frontend/API 404, and Development API database-health 503 for missing/unreachable DB.
- Edge desktop/360 px checks passed. Visual Studio GUI opening and MySQL Workbench GUI import remain unverified.

## 1.1.0.3 DataModel — 2026-10-29

Branch: `CommentsService/v_1.1.0.3_DataModel`

- Added OOP Author/Comment entities, EF Core 10/PostgreSQL mappings, UUID keys, UTC timestamps and IPv4/IPv6/User-Agent metadata.
- Added initial migration 20261029195935_InitialDataModel with schema/history, required fields, length/check constraints, restricted author deletion and indexes.
- Wired the application to its non-superuser database role; added explicit migrate/check commands and database health. Startup does not migrate automatically.
- Added restore-verified checkpoints that retain one previous copy per database and remove only their own temporary verification databases.
- Added eight integration tests using per-test transaction rollback; no database reset or shared-table cleanup.
- Added PostgreSQL SQL export, ER/OOP diagrams, a MySQL Workbench import projection and migration/recovery documentation.
- Updated three READMEs, read.me and plans. Comment APIs, replies and attachments remain in their planned iterations; configuration version stays 0.
- Isolated Windows/Linux intermediate build assets; included tests in the solution. Added the runtime GSS library while retaining default driver encryption settings.
- Validation: Ubuntu Release solution build passed with zero warnings/errors; 8/8 PostgreSQL tests passed; Docker backend/frontend builds and all three services are healthy.
- Verified restore of both pre-migration checkpoints, retained control data across initial migration, and unchanged author/comment data/relationships across repeated migration.
- Verified restoration of related author/comment checkpoint fixtures, separate blank-database installation, idempotent PostgreSQL SQL export and unchanged persistent volumes.
- Verified image migration/check commands, native API startup without DB credentials (database health 503), Windows localhost access, and Edge desktop/360 px layout with correct release/status and no JavaScript errors.
- MySQL Workbench GUI import and opening the updated solution in Visual Studio were not verified. The SQL projection and import instructions are supplied.

## 1.1.0.2 VisualStudio — 2026-10-29

Branch: `CommentsService/v_1.1.0.2_VisualStudio`

- Added CommentsService.slnx for opening the existing API and React files in Visual Studio 2026.
- Frontend files are solution items; building the solution builds the API. Docker still builds the complete application.
